## effect not in signature
V3001 7:4 function `f` performs `Console`, which its signature does not allow (allowed: `{}`)
  Cause 7:18 `Console.print("x")` `Console.print` performs `Console` here
  expected: {}
  actual: {Console}
  fix (Suggested, InterfaceChange): Add `Console` to the signature " ! {Console}"
  fix (Incomplete, Local): Handle the effect locally with `with` "{ with ?handler " " }"

## fail not in signature
V3001 7:4 function `f` performs `Fail<A>`, which its signature does not allow (allowed: `{}`)
  Cause 7:17 `fail A` `fail` performs `Fail<A>` here
  expected: {}
  actual: {Fail<A>}
  fix (Suggested, InterfaceChange): Add `Fail<A>` to the signature " ! {Fail<A>}"
  fix (Incomplete, Local): Recover from the failure locally with `try`/`catch` "{ try " " catch { _ => ?recover } }"

## wrong fail tag
V3001 7:4 function `f` performs `Fail<B>`, which its signature does not allow (allowed: `{Fail<A>}`)
  Cause 7:29 `fail B` `fail` performs `Fail<B>` here
  expected: {Fail<A>}
  actual: {Fail<B>}
  fix (Suggested, InterfaceChange): Add `Fail<B>` to the signature "{Fail<A | B>}"
  fix (Incomplete, Local): Recover from the failure locally with `try`/`catch` "{ try " " catch { _ => ?recover } }"

## rigid row variable is not empty
V3001 7:4 the body of `f` performs the effects of `e`, which its signature `{}` does not allow
  expected: {}
  actual: e
  fix (Suggested, InterfaceChange): Add the row variable `e` to the signature " ! e"

